+Origin: phase-04 code-reviewer round 4, item 4, and human decision 2026-10-27, row 5. The hadoop-engineer role file requires a local bounded run, the guard blocks `sbt run` and `runMain`, and plain `java` was unguarded. hadoop-engineer ran `java @<argfile> <Main> ...`, and nothing checked it. This section replaces that gap with one form that the guard can check from the command text alone. There is no wrapper script (the round-1 `scripts/run-local-main.sh` proposal is withdrawn).
+
+Rule R7C-MAIN. Only `hadoop-engineer` (`LOCAL_MAIN_AGENT`) may launch a JVM directly, and only in this form, as one simple command run from the repository root:
+
+`java [-Xmx<n>[k|m|g]] [-Xms<n>[k|m|g]] -cp "<classpath>" <main-class> <arguments...> [> <file>] [2> <file>] [2>&1]`
+
+| Main class (`local_main_out_arg`) | Output base argument | Every other path argument |
+|---|---|---|
+| `edu.uic.cs441.scholarchain.hadoop.DblpPipelineMain` | argument 3 | input |
+| `edu.uic.cs441.scholarchain.hadoop.SourcePipelineMain` | argument 1 | input |
+| any other class, any other agent, the orchestrator | blocked until an amendment adds a row | |
+
+What the guard checks (mechanical, on the words bash builds: quoted parts joined, unquoted backslashes dropped):
+1. One simple command. Outside quotes there is no `;`, `|`, `&&`, `||`, `(`, `)`, `$`, backtick, `<`, `#`, `~`, `{`, `}`, `[`, `]`, `*`, `?`, or newline. Inside double quotes there is no `$` or backtick, and nowhere inside quotes is there a `>` or `&`. The only `&` allowed is in `>&1` or `>&2`. So there is no `cd`, pipe, prefix assignment (`VAR=value java`), command substitution, or second command.
+2. The command word is exactly `java` or `java.exe` on PATH. It is not a path, a variable, or a wrapper such as `env`, `timeout`, `bash -c`, or `xargs`.
+3. JVM options are only one `-cp`, `-classpath`, or `--class-path`, plus optional `-Xmx<n>` and `-Xms<n>`. No `-D`, `-jar`, `-javaagent`, `-agentlib`, `--module-path`, `-XX`, or `@argfile`.
+4. Classpath entries are split at `;`. Each one must exist, must not be a wildcard, and must be either the compiled classes directory of a module in `LOCAL_MAIN_CP_MODULES` (`core` and `hadoop`: `modules/<m>/target/scala-*/classes`, never `test-classes`) or a `.jar` file in the Coursier cache (`COURSIER_CACHE`, `%LOCALAPPDATA%/Coursier/Cache`, `~/.cache/coursier`). Both the normalized path and its realpath must match.
+5. Program arguments are positional only: no word may start with `-`. The output base argument must resolve strictly inside the scratchpad or a temp directory (`TEMP`, `TMP`, `TMPDIR`, `/tmp`), outside the repository, with no glob characters. Its nearest existing ancestor must still be inside after realpath, which covers junctions, symlinks, and 8.3 names.
+6. Every other path-like argument (one that contains `/` or `\`, starts with `.` or `file:`, has a drive letter, or contains `{ } [ ]`) is an input. It must resolve strictly inside `datasets/samples/` and exist, both normalized and after realpath. A Hadoop glob may use `{a,b}` or `[...]` only in the last component, inside quotes, and its directory must exist. `*` and `?` are never allowed, because the Windows java launcher expands them itself and shifts the positional arguments (phase-04 run report, command 3).
+7. A bare argument (snapshot ID, run ID, number) must not name an existing path in the working directory, `CLAUDE.md`, or `human-gate.md`. No argument may contain `$`, a backtick, `~`, `<`, `>`, or `&`, or be empty. Remote schemes (`s3:`, `s3a:`, `hdfs:`, `http(s):`, `abfs:`, `gs:`, `jdbc:`, any `scheme://` other than `file:`) and `file://host` are blocked. `file:///C:/...` and `file:/...` are allowed and resolved as local paths.
+8. Redirect targets resolve strictly inside the scratchpad or a temp directory, like the output base.
+9. R4-PROTNORM (section 7b, `ds_prot_hit`) also runs on the whole command.
+10. A command that passes gets `permissionDecision: ask` from the guard itself. The flag is set by the check, not by a text pattern (amendment review F4), so the human approves every run, whatever its spelling. There is no settings.json allow rule for `java`.
