+
+Rule R7C-JVM, the launcher fence (every caller, the orchestrator included). Every other direct JVM or cluster launch is blocked: `java`, `javaw`, `javac`, `jdb`, `jshell`, `jrunscript`, `jjs`, `scala`, `scala3`, `scalac`, `scala-cli`, `amm`, `jbang`, `kotlin`, `kotlinc`, `groovy`, `coursier`, `cs`, `mvn`, `mvnw`, `gradle`, `gradlew`, `spark-submit`, `spark-shell`, `spark-class`, `spark-sql`, `pyspark`, `sparkR`, `hadoop`, `yarn`, `mapred`, and `hdfs` (`JVM_LAUNCHERS`).
+- Where it applies: as the command word in any path, `.exe`, `.cmd`, or `.bat` form, after `VAR=value` prefixes and shell keywords. It applies after the wrappers in `JVM_WRAP` (`env`, `timeout`, `nice`, `sudo`, `flock`, `xargs`, `cmd`, `pwsh`, `wsl`, and others), whose options and option arguments are skipped. It applies as the target of `find -exec`, and inside `bash -c`, `eval`, `env -S`, `cmd /c`, `pwsh -c`, and `su -c` strings. A launcher named as `bin/<name>` or `<name>.exe/.cmd/.bat` anywhere after a wrapper is blocked too.
+- Also blocked: a command word that is a glob (`/c/*/bin/jav?.exe`), and a variable command word that names java, jdk, jre, hadoop, spark, scala, and similar tools (`"$(which java)"`).
+- Allowed: version queries (`java -version`, `--version`, `-fullversion`, `-showversion`; `hadoop version`; `hadoop checknative [-a]`; `yarn|mapred|hdfs version`; `<launcher> --version`).
